# AgentManager — local development environment.
#
# Copy to `.env` and populate. `.env` is git-ignored (foundation DESIGN §3.5);
# this example is the only env file that is ever committed.
#
# DEVELOPMENT AND TESTS ONLY. The installed service never reads this file: it
# reads `claude.oauthToken` from the DPAPI secret store, written by
# scripts/Setup-Auth.ps1. Populating this is not a substitute for that.
#
# Read by `npm run test:live` only (node --env-file-if-exists=.env). `npm test`
# and `npm run ci` do not load it, so a token sitting here can never quietly
# turn the ordinary suite into a run that spends plan quota.

# The Claude subscription token, from `claude setup-token`.
#
# Gates the live SDK checks — 19 of them across runner/__spike__ (SDK-NOTES
# §11, L1–L16), orchestrator/__spike__ (§10, L1–L15) and roster's
# draft.live.test.ts. They `describe.skipIf(!hasToken)` without it. These are
# real turns against your plan: running them costs quota.
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=

# SDK-NOTES L12 — the auth-failure check, the 20th gated test. Off by default
# because it is a deliberate failure and the others are not. It strips every
# credential from the child environment itself, so leaving the token above
# populated is fine and changes nothing about what it proves.
#AGENTMANAGER_SPIKE_AUTH_FAILURE=1

# Never set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY here (architecture D2). It silently overrides
# subscription auth for every process started afterwards, so the token above
# would be ignored while it is present — the same trap Setup-Auth.ps1 warns
# about for the user and machine scopes.
